040522 Update - JunkerIn

All has gone fine. My first site had one lack -- only one SQL dbase was there. Most of the installables use one, so today I went to the Ace site to find out how and cost for more dbases.

Upon arrival, I saw a new special -- 2000 MB Disk Space, 60 GB Bandwidth, Unlimited SQLs, As low as $3.95 (for, I assume a 2 year contract like mine)...

So, a few minutes later, click, ckick, service ticket, I upgraded for $1/mo or $24 totoal for my total contract of 2 years. My site immediately showed the upgrade. All done in a few minutes.

So here it is again with a listing of the automatic software installs. I don't know what half of them do, but they are all free software projects on the web and have their own sites with tons of info.

- - -

2000 MB Disk Space, 60 GB Bandwidth, Unlimited <nowiki>MySQL</nowiki>, Unlimited Email, POP3/SMTP/IMAP, <nowiki>WebMail</nowiki> Access, SPAM Assassin, <nowiki>MySQL</nowiki> & PHP, Perl & CGI-Bin, 24/7 FTP Access, Easy Control Panel, Auto-install Scripts, Free Templates, Free Software

Auto-Install Scripts via Fantastico:

Navigation - Fantastico Home, Control Panel Home, 

Blogs - b2, b2evolution, Nucleus, pMachine Free, <nowiki>WordPress</nowiki>

Content Management - Drupal, Geeklog, Mambo Open Source, PHP-Nuke, <nowiki>phpWCMS, phpWebSite</nowiki>, Post-Nuke, Siteframe, Xoops 

Customer Support - Crafty Syntax Live Help, Help Center Live, <nowiki>osTicket</nowiki>, PHP Support Tickets, Support Logic Helpdesk, Support Services Manager
 
Discussion Boards - Invision Board, <nowiki>phpBB2, YaBBSE</nowiki>
 
E-Commerce - <nowiki>CubeCart</nowiki>, OS Commerce
 
F.A.Q. - <nowiki>FAQMasterFlex</nowiki>
 
Image Galleries - 4Images Gallery, Coppermine Photo Gallery, Gallery 
 
Mailing Lists - <nowiki>PHPlist</nowiki>
 
Polls and Surveys - Advanced Poll, <nowiki>phpESP, PHPSurveyor</nowiki>
 
Project Management - <nowiki>dotProject, PHProjekt</nowiki>
 
Wiki - <nowiki>PhpWiki, TikiWiki</nowiki>
 
Other Scripts - Moodle, Noahs Classifieds, Open-Realty, <nowiki>phpAdsNew, PHPauction, phpCOIN, phpFormGenerator, phpLinks, WebCalendar</nowiki>
 
Extras - Language, Side menu appearance, Email notifications, Installations overview

- - -

UPDATE - 040327, JunkerIn. No problems. All works as should.

So, $110.80 for two years ($4.62/mo). My domain name had now spread and I can access the control panel. Here it is:

