Control panel documentation Table of Contents, Part 1: General

What is CPanel?, How do I get help?, CPanel themes, General server information, Mail, <nowiki>NeoMail</nowiki> summary, Horde summary, <nowiki>SquirrelMail</nowiki> summary, Setting your default e-mail address, Autoresponders, E-mail Filtering, Forwarders, Mailing Lists, Spam Assassin, Tracing an e-mail address, Altering your Mail Exchanger (MX Entry) setting, Change Password, Parked Domains, Addon Domains, FTP Manager, Setting Anonymous FTP access, File Manager, Changing file/folder permissions, <nowiki>Generating/Restoring</nowiki> backups, Password protect directories, Subdomains, <nowiki>MySQL</nowiki>, Managing <nowiki>MySQL</nowiki> databases, Adding host access, <nowiki>PostgreSQL</nowiki>, Managing <nowiki>PostgreSQL</nowiki> databases, SSL <nowiki>Shell/Telnet</nowiki> access, Redirects, <nowiki>Web/FTP</nowiki> Stats, Search Engine Submit, Chatroom, <nowiki>PhpMyChat</nowiki>, Bulletin Board

Control panel documentation Table of Contents, Part 2: The CGI Center

Introduction to CGI, Simple CGI Wrappper, Random HTML, Guestbook, Advanced Guestbook, Counter Maker, CGI EMail, <nowiki>FormMail</nowiki> Clone, Entropy Search, Entropy Banner, Scripts Library, Interchange shopping cart, Agora Shopping Cart, Cron jobs, Network Tools, Domain Lookup, Trace Route, MIME Types, Apache handlers, Manage <nowiki>OpenPGP</nowiki> keys, <nowiki>HotLink</nowiki> Prevention, Index Manager, IP Deny Manager, Index

Control panel documentation Table of Contents, notes:

:<nowiki>NeoMail</nowiki> summary - online mail function
:Horde summary - <nowiki>SquirrelMail/Horde</nowiki> is a full-featured e-mail application, http://www.horde.org/
:<nowiki>SquirrelMail</nowiki> summary - a full-featured e-mail application, http://www.squirrelmail.org/
:Default e-mail address - unknowns rerouted to your default: user@yourdomain.com
:Mailing Lists - a mailing list, http://www.gnu.org/software/mailman/mailman.html
:Spam Assassin - a mail filter, http://spamassassin.taint.org/index.html
:Tracing an e-mail address - trace the delivery path of an e-mail address

:Subdomains - subdom.yourdom.com, on your master account. But, no new CPanel. a sub folder within public_http with it's own cgi-bin. Currently no e-mail accounts, but a workaround is name-subdom@yourdom.com or similar.

:SSL <nowiki>Shell/Telnet</nowiki> access - log in, linux your domain: uses "<nowiki>MindTerm</nowiki>" http://www.appgate.com/mindterm/, get "<nowiki>PuTTy</nowiki>" - http://www.appgate.com/mindterm/ - an excellent <nowiki>Telnet/SSL</nowiki> utility: small; fast; and free (for Windows).

:Chatroom - Entropy Chat is a simple chat script that offers basic features.
:<nowiki>PhpMyChat</nowiki> - PHP chat room uses <nowiki>MySQL</nowiki> database, see http://www.phpheaven.net/rubrique4.html
:Bulletin Board - install a pre-made forum called phpBB, see http://www.phpbb.com/

More on CGI Center is to come.

- - -next step, 040128,  JunkerIn

Docs > Bulletin Board > "Click on the Icon"

Clicked on the Icon > "Type in a sub-diectory name" > "Hit Go"

AND...

my *Powered by phpBB 2.0.6 © 2001, 2002 phpBB Group* was up and running.

/////

And there it was. If you've seen a phpBB on the net, that is what it looks and works like. It uses one of <nowiki>MySQLs</nowiki>, my only one. Is that OK? Will I need more? What do they cost? But that was sure easy and the product looks fine.

040327, note: Still no idea on SQL use, haven't had a need to track it down yet. Also, started new svc for old domain name with a requested transfer of name. Transfer generated two emails requesting confirmation from current admin of domain name. Answered 'yes' to each. New service came up with no problem. I FTP-ed my HTML files and the transfer was completed. No problem. --JunkerIn.

- - -

